  "headline": "The Statistical Relevance Fallacy",
  "alternativeHeadline": "Why Probabilistic Confidence Cannot Substitute for Structural Verification",
  "description": "Vector similarity and next-token probability measure linguistic proximity, not factual truth or legal compliance. In enterprise customer storytelling and regulated developer platforms, compositive AI pipelines must gate probabilistic outputs behind deterministic thresholds and human-approved source receipts.",
